            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24791-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24791 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The net/http HTTP/1.1 client mishandled the case where a server responds to a request with an \"Expect: 100-continue\" header with a non-informational (200 or higher) status. This mishandling could leave a client connection in an invalid state, where the next request sent on the connection will fail. An attacker sending a request to a net/http/httputil.ReverseProxy proxy can exploit this mishandling to cause a denial of service by sending \"Expect: 100-continue\" requests which elicit a non-informational response from the backend. Each such request leaves the proxy with an invalid connection, and causes one subsequent request using that connection to fail."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.21.12,1.22.5\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-24791](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-24791**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.21.12,1.22.5  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-24791](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24791)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-24785-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-24785 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If errors returned from MarshalJSON methods contain user controlled data, they may be used to break the contextual auto-escaping behavior of the html/template package, allowing for subsequent actions to inject unexpected content into templates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-24785\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.21.8,1.22.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-24785](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24785)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-24785**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.21.8,1.22.1  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-24785](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-24785)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-24538-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-24538 critical vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Templates do not properly consider backticks (`) as Javascript string delimiters, and do not escape them as expected. Backticks are used, since ES6, for JS template literals. If a template contains a Go template action within a Javascript template literal, the contents of the action can be used to terminate the literal, injecting arbitrary Javascript code into the Go template. As ES6 template literals are rather complex, and themselves can do string interpolation, the decision was made to simply disallow Go template actions from being used inside of them (e.g. \"var a = {{.}}\"), since there is no obviously safe way to allow this behavior. This takes the same approach as github.com/google/safehtml. With fix, Template.Parse returns an Error when it encounters templates like this, with an ErrorCode of value 12. This ErrorCode is currently unexported, but will be exported in the release of Go 1.21. Users who rely on the previous behavior can re-enable it using the GODEBUG flag jstmpllitinterp=1, with the caveat that backticks will now be escaped. This should be used with caution."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-24538\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.19.8,1.20.3\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-24538](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24538)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-24538**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.19.8,1.20.3  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-24538](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-24538)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
