            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29405-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29405 critical vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The go command may execute arbitrary code at build time when using cgo. This may occur when running \"go get\" on a malicious module, or when running any other command which builds untrusted code. This is can by triggered by linker flags, specified via a \"#cgo LDFLAGS\" directive. Flags containing embedded spaces are mishandled, allowing disallowed flags to be smuggled through the LDFLAGS sanitization by including them in the argument of another flag. This only affects usage of the gccgo compiler."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-29405\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.19.10,1.20.5\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-29405](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-29405)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-29405**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.19.10,1.20.5  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-29405](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-29405)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-29227-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-29227 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a cloud-native high-performance edge/middle/service proxy. In versions prior to 1.22.1 if Envoy attempts to send an internal redirect of an HTTP request consisting of more than HTTP headers, there’s a lifetime bug which can be triggered. If while replaying the request Envoy sends a local reply when the redirect headers are processed, the downstream state indicates that the downstream stream is not complete. On sending the local reply, Envoy will attempt to reset the upstream stream, but as it is actually complete, and deleted, this result in a use-after-free. Users are advised to upgrade. Users unable to upgrade are advised to disable internal redirects if crashes are observed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-29227\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2022-29227](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-29227)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-29227**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.22.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2022-29227](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-29227)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-29228-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-29228 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a cloud-native high-performance proxy. In versions prior to 1.22.1 the OAuth filter would try to invoke the remaining filters in the chain after emitting a local response, which triggers an ASSERT() in newer versions and corrupts memory on earlier versions. continueDecoding() shouldn’t ever be called from filters after a local reply has been sent. Users are advised to upgrade. There are no known workarounds for this issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-29228\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2022-29228](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-29228)",
