            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-35945-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-35945 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a cloud-native high-performance edge/middle/service proxy. Envoy’s HTTP/2 codec may leak a header map and bookkeeping structures upon receiving `RST_STREAM` immediately followed by the `GOAWAY` frames from an upstream server. In nghttp2, cleanup of pending requests due to receipt of the `GOAWAY` frame skips de-allocation of the bookkeeping structure and pending compressed header. The error return [code path] is taken if connection is already marked for not sending more requests due to `GOAWAY` frame. The clean-up code is right after the return statement, causing memory leak. Denial of service through memory exhaustion. This vulnerability was patched in versions(s) 1.26.3, 1.25.8, 1.24.9, 1.23.11."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-35945\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.23.11,1.24.9,1.25.8,1.26.3\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-35945](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-35945)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-35945**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.23.11,1.24.9,1.25.8,1.26.3  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-35945](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-35945)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
