            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-23326-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-23326 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a cloud-native, open source edge and service proxy. A theoretical request smuggling vulnerability exists through Envoy if a server can be tricked into adding an upgrade header into a response. Per RFC https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7230#section-6.7 a server sends 101 when switching protocols. Envoy incorrectly accepts a 200 response from a server when requesting a protocol upgrade, but 200 does not indicate protocol switch. This opens up the possibility of request smuggling through Envoy if the server can be tricked into adding the upgrade header to the response."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-23326\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.27.6,1.28.4,1.29.5,1.30.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2024-23326](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-23326)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-23326**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.27.6,1.28.4,1.29.5,1.30.2  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2024-23326](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-23326)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-29409-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-29409 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Extremely large RSA keys in certificate chains can cause a client/server to expend significant CPU time verifying signatures. With fix, the size of RSA keys transmitted during handshakes is restricted to \u003c= 8192 bits. Based on a survey of publicly trusted RSA keys, there are currently only three certificates in circulation with keys larger than this, and all three appear to be test certificates that are not actively deployed. It is possible there are larger keys in use in private PKIs, but we target the web PKI, so causing breakage here in the interests of increasing the default safety of users of crypto/tls seems reasonable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-29409\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.19.12,1.20.7\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-29409](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-29409)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-29409**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.19.12,1.20.7  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-29409](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-29409)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39318-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39318 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not properly handle HTML-like \"\" comment tokens, nor hashbang \"#!\" comment tokens, in \u003cscript\u003e contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly interpret the contents of \u003cscript\u003e contexts, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This may be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-39318\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.20.8,1.21.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-39318](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-39318)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-39318**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.17.7  | 1.20.8,1.21.1  | go-module  | /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-39318](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-39318)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39319-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39319 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The html/template package does not apply the proper rules for handling occurrences of \"\u003cscript\", \"\u003c!--\", and \"\u003c/script\" within JS literals in \u003cscript\u003e contexts. This may cause the template parser to improperly consider script contexts to be terminated early, causing actions to be improperly escaped. This could be leveraged to perform an XSS attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-39319\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.20.8,1.21.1\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-39319](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-39319)",
