            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27496-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27496 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is an open source edge and service proxy designed for cloud-native applications. Prior to versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9, the OAuth filter assumes that a `state` query param is present on any response that looks like an OAuth redirect response. Sending it a request with the URI path equivalent to the redirect path, without the `state` parameter, will lead to abnormal termination of Envoy process. Versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9 contain a patch. The issue can also be mitigated by locking down OAuth traffic, disabling the filter, or by filtering traffic before it reaches the OAuth filter (e.g. via a lua script)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-27496\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-27496](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27496)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-27496**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-27496](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27496)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27487-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27487 critical vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is an open source edge and service proxy designed for cloud-native applications. Prior to versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9, the client may bypass JSON Web Token (JWT) checks and forge fake original paths. The header `x-envoy-original-path` should be an internal header, but Envoy does not remove this header from the request at the beginning of request processing when it is sent from an untrusted client. The faked header would then be used for trace logs and grpc logs, as well as used in the URL used for `jwt_authn` checks if the `jwt_authn` filter is used, and any other upstream use of the x-envoy-original-path header. Attackers may forge a trusted `x-envoy-original-path` header. Versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9 have patches for this issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-27487\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-27487](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27487)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-27487**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-27487](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27487)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
