            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27491-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27491 critical vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is an open source edge and service proxy designed for cloud-native applications. Compliant HTTP/1 service should reject malformed request lines. Prior to versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9, There is a possibility that non compliant HTTP/1 service may allow malformed requests, potentially leading to a bypass of security policies. This issue is fixed in versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-27491\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-27491](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27491)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-27491**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-27491](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27491)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-41715-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-41715 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Programs which compile regular expressions from untrusted sources may be vulnerable to memory exhaustion or denial of service. The parsed regexp representation is linear in the size of the input, but in some cases the constant factor can be as high as 40,000, making relatively small regexps consume much larger amounts of memory. After fix, each regexp being parsed is limited to a 256 MB memory footprint. Regular expressions whose representation would use more space than that are rejected. Normal use of regular expressions is unaffected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-41715\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.18.7,1.19.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2022-41715](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2022-41715)",
