            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-27493-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-27493 critical vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is an open source edge and service proxy designed for cloud-native applications. Prior to versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9, Envoy does not sanitize or escape request properties when generating request headers. This can lead to characters that are illegal in header values to be sent to the upstream service. In the worst case, it can cause upstream service to interpret the original request as two pipelined requests, possibly bypassing the intent of Envoy’s security policy. Versions 1.26.0, 1.25.3, 1.24.4, 1.23.6, and 1.22.9 contain a patch. As a workaround, disable adding request headers based on the downstream request properties, such as downstream certificate properties."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-27493\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-27493](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27493)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-27493**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.22.9,1.23.6,1.24.4,1.25.3  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-27493](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-27493)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-47907-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-47907 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Cancelling a query (e.g. by cancelling the context passed to one of the query methods) during a call to the Scan method of the returned Rows can result in unexpected results if other queries are being made in parallel. This can result in a race condition that may overwrite the expected results with those of another query, causing the call to Scan to return either unexpected results from the other query or an error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-47907\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.17.7\nFix Version: 1.23.12,1.24.6\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/pilot-agent\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-47907](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-47907)",
