              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-62409-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-62409 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a cloud-native, open source edge and service proxy. Prior to 1.36.1, 1.35.5, 1.34.9, and 1.33.10, large requests and responses can potentially trigger TCP connection pool crashes due to flow control management in Envoy. It will happen when the connection is closing but upstream data is still coming, resulting in a buffer watermark callback nullptr reference. The vulnerability impacts TCP proxy and HTTP 1 \u0026 2 mixed use cases based on ALPN. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.36.1, 1.35.5, 1.34.9, and 1.33.10."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-62409\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.33.10,1.34.9,1.35.5,1.36.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-62409](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-62409)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-62409**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.33.10,1.34.9,1.35.5,1.36.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-62409](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-62409)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/envoy@1.21.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-58183-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-58183 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tar.Reader does not set a maximum size on the number of sparse region data blocks in GNU tar pax 1.0 sparse files. A maliciously-crafted archive containing a large number of sparse regions can cause a Reader to read an unbounded amount of data from the archive into memory. When reading from a compressed source, a small compressed input can result in large allocations."
