            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-26308-envoy",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-26308 high vulnerability for envoy package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Envoy is a high-performance edge/middle/service proxy. Prior to 1.37.1, 1.36.5, 1.35.8, and 1.34.13, the Envoy RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) filter contains a logic vulnerability in how it validates HTTP headers when multiple values are present for the same header name. Instead of validating each header value individually, Envoy concatenates all values into a single comma-separated string. This behavior allows attackers to bypass RBAC policies—specifically \"Deny\" rules—by sending duplicate headers, effectively obscuring the malicious value from exact-match mechanisms. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.37.1, 1.36.5, 1.35.8, and 1.34.13."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-26308\nSeverity: high\nPackage: envoy\nVersion: 1.21.0\nFix Version: 1.34.13,1.35.9,1.36.5,1.37.1\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/bin/envoy\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-26308](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26308)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-26308**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | envoy  | 1.21.0  | 1.34.13,1.35.9,1.36.5,1.37.1  | binary  | /usr/local/bin/envoy  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-26308](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-26308)  |\n"
              },
